<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
	Anomaly-style magic research: the deeper Rimworld of Magic research tree is funded from
	a TM_ArcaneKnowledge pool (see Defs\KnowledgeCategoryDefs\TM_KnowledgeCategories.xml)
	instead of a research bench. That pool is filled by studying at the magic circle
	buildings (Patches\TM_StudyMagicCircles.xml) or by reading grimoires, Tome-style
	(Patches\TM_GrimoireTomeResearch.xml). Every TM_* project in this tree is now
	knowledge-only except TM_ArcaneConstruction, which is left on bench baseCost purely for
	structural reasons (nothing else needs its cost model changed - it's moot either way).
	TM_ArcaneConstruction and TM_ArcaneFundamentals are force-finished at game start
	regardless of scenario (Source\NoobsFixes.RWoMFix), so a colony always starts with basic
	arcane research done and can immediately build the small magic circle to start
	generating knowledge from nothing, with no grimoire required.
	knowledgeCost values below are baseCost/100 (min 5), matching vanilla Anomaly's typical
	knowledgeCost range.

	Every project below also gets a <generalRules> block (subject/subject_story/
	subject_gerund rulesStrings), because BookOutcomeProperties_GainResearch (the base
	class vanilla's own Tome doer, and ours, both use - see
	Patches\TM_GrimoireTomeResearch.xml) hard-requires generalRules != null in its internal
	IsValid() check (confirmed by decompiling Assembly-CSharp.dll's
	RimWorld.ReadingOutcomeDoerGainResearch). Without this, EVERY TM_* project fails that
	check, OnBookGenerated() finds zero valid targets, and reading a grimoire grants no
	knowledge at all - these rules exist purely to satisfy that requirement, not for UI
	flavor (though they do also feed the book's generated description text).
-->
<Patch>

	<!-- TM_ArcaneFundamentals: baseCost 300 -> knowledgeCost 5
	     (moot in practice: TM_ArcaneFundamentals is force-finished at game start by the
	     Harmony patch in Source\NoobsFixes.RWoMFix, same as TM_ArcaneConstruction) -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
				<xpath>Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName = "TM_ArcaneFundamentals"]/baseCost</xpath>
			</li>
			<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/ResearchProjectDef[defName = "TM_ArcaneFundamentals"]</xpath>
				<value>
					<knowledgeCost>5</knowledgeCost>
					<knowledgeCategory>TM_ArcaneKnowledge</knowledgeCategory>
					<generalRules>
						<rulesStrings>
							<li>subject->arcane fundamentals</li>
							<li>subject_story->puzzled out the mathematics linking arcane power to the physical realm</li>
							<li>subject_gerund->unraveling arcane fundamentals</li>
						</rulesStrings>
					</generalRules>
				</value>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

